<package xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <metadata>
    <id>womic</id>
    <title>WO Mic</title>
    <version>6.4</version>
    <authors>Wolicheng</authors>
    <owners>chocolatey-community</owners>
    <summary>Turn your phone into a microphone for your computer</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[WO Mic can turn your phone to be a microphone for your computer. You do not need to pay a cent to buy a gadget. And it's mobile if you choose wireless transport. Millions of people have installed it and are using it daily for talking, recording, voice remote control and many other activities.

## Features

- Wireless microphone without any cost
- Can be used with any programs on PC just like REAL microphone
- Very short lag
- Easy to configure and use
- Supports auto reconnection when your PC reboots
- Support multiple connection methods: USB, Bluetooth, Wi-Fi, and Wi-Fi direct
- Audio format: 48000 sampling rate, 16 bits per sample, mono channel

## Package Parameters

- None

## Notes

- This package installs the WO Mic client and virtual device driver on Windows
- Requires VC runtime re-distributable (x86) which is automatically installed
- You also need to install the WO Mic app on your phone (Android/iOS)
- If you have security concerns, check the [WO Mic website](https://wolicheng.com/womic/) for more information

]]></description>
    <projectUrl>https://wolicheng.com/womic/</projectUrl>
    <packageSourceUrl>https://github.com/chocolatey-community/chocolatey-packages/tree/master/automatic/womic</packageSourceUrl>
